<section class="hero compact">
    <p class="eyebrow">EMERALD / SYSTEM INSTALLATION</p>
    <h1>xchroot</h1>

    <p class="lead">
        Enter a Vylen installation target with the filesystems and DNS context
        required for package administration.
    </p>

    <div class="command-line"># xchroot &lt;chroot-dir&gt; [command]</div>
</section>

<section class="doc">
    <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>

    <pre><code>xchroot /mnt
xchroot /mnt portsync
xchroot /mnt emerald sysup -y
xchroot /mnt /usr/bin/bash</code></pre>

    <p>
        Without a command, xchroot starts <code>/usr/bin/sh</code> inside the
        target. Arguments after the directory are passed to the command unchanged.
    </p>

    <h2 id="mounts">Mounts</h2>

    <p>
        The helper mounts <code>/dev</code>, <code>/dev/pts</code>,
        <code>/dev/shm</code>, <code>/proc</code>, <code>/run</code>,
        <code>/sys</code>, optional EFI variables, <code>/tmp</code>, and the
        host <code>/etc/resolv.conf</code>. Mounts that are already present are
        left alone.
    </p>

    <h2 id="sessions">Sessions</h2>

    <p>
        Several xchroot sessions can share the same target. Only the last session
        to exit unmounts the filesystems. The target can't be the host root
        <code>/</code>, and the command must be run as root.
    </p>
</section>
